<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yujiulü Chounu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 520</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yujiulü Chounu was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> of the Rouran from 508 to 520. He succeeded his father Futu, who had been killed by the Gaoche, and in 516 he defeated and killed the Gaoche king Mi'etu. He sent envoys to the Northern Wei, among them a Buddhist monk in 511. He was killed in 520 in a conflict at his court, and his brother Anagui succeeded him.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Religion combined steppe cults of Heaven with shamanic practices, and Buddhism also reached the court: in 511 the khagan <b>Chounu</b> sent a monk as his envoy to the Northern Wei.</blockquote><a href="/empire/rouran-khaganate">Rouran Khaganate · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
